+**New structural no-go theorem (October 19, 2026).**
+[Large winning-state frontier](docs/research-winning-frontier-barrier.md) constructs,
+on an infinite family of sizes `n`, `2^(Omega(n log^2 n))` pairwise
+nonisomorphic reachable partial orders that are **actually sortable** within
+the remaining information-bound budget. This excludes algorithms that explicitly
+enumerate *all* winning states even after extension-count pruning and symmetry
+quotienting; it is **not** a lower bound on the running time of computing `S(n)`.
+The paper proof is not yet Lean-checked.
+
 The reference minimax evaluator is `scripts/evaluate.py` (exact for small `n`).
 
 The [development contract](AGENTS.md) makes this priority explicit for agents.
